These may be spoilers...




















I'm trying to figure out the best way of robbing a shop. I found a nice
wand shop in Discover mode, so I collected all the wands, found a wand
of digging, and tried to dig through the floor. The shopkeeper jumped
from the other side of the room, grabbed my backpack (?? All my wands
and stuff), fell through the floor with me, and toasted me with all the
wands he stole from me. (Well, I *had* stolen them from him first, right?)

Teleporting things out doesn't work either, you get charged.

So, apart from having your pet steal for you (this works well, but I 
often ditch my pet or it gets killed by a falling rock trap) this is
what I do:
   You need a wand of teleportation with a few charges. Get all the stuff you
want, and when you're ready... zap the shopkeeper with the wand of
teleportation. Then run like hell toward the down staircase. Usew telepathy
(you probably need this, too) and if the shopkeeper is between you and the
down staircase, zap him when he's a few squares away. You will have a real
pissed off shopkeeper, so pray your wand doesn't run out of charges. Get 
down those stairs, and don't come back until your more powerful. This method
has the advantage of no Keystone Kops generated. The disadvantage? If
your wands run out of charges, watch out...
    Another suggestion: Throw a potion of paralysis at the shopkeeper, and
try to dig through the floor. I never tried this, though.

